※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4579

※ A record's fields have names and its value uses them, so that a value reads as
※ what it is rather than as a list whose order has to be checked against the
※ definition.  A tuple is the shape for several values that go by position, and
※ is what a program wanting that should write.

type Point = x : u32 ; y : u32

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let p : Point = Point(1u32, 2u32)
    if p.x = 1u32: 0u6 else: 1u6
